"""Recorded `nsys stats --format csv` exports for lab 28. Synthesized, not measured.

No GPU wrote these files. A script chose the kernel durations, the gaps, and the
API call times so that each export tells one consistent story on an A100 80GB
PCIe. The layouts follow `nsys stats --report cuda_gpu_trace` and
`--report cuda_api_sum`: a progress line, then a header and one row per record.
The column set differs between Nsight Systems versions, so read a column by its
header name. Do not edit this file.

    LAUNCH_BOUND   60 kernels of about 3 microseconds, issued one launch at a time
    SYNC_BOUND     12 steps of a 350 microsecond kernel and a 4-byte copy, then a host pause
    OVERLAP        two streams, each busy, running at the same time
"""

